("ADV-026",NC,"'Meanwhile' starts a new sentence. To join two clauses, use 'while'.","MEAN-WHILE: in the WHILE between.","'In the meantime' means the same.","Write two sentences using 'Meanwhile' to link them.",None,"meanwhile vs while","While + clause joins two things (while she cooked, he cleaned). Meanwhile starts a new sentence."),
